    "explanation": "Summary for both parties: a route deviation is established on this trip, but the only evidence that fixes the distance is a GPS trace the platform has down-weighted to 0.30, so no ruling can be issued at the 0.70 confidence the rules require. The case goes to a human reviewer and the disputed SGD 12.00 is held — neither collected nor refunded.\n\nWhat is agreed. The platform's route was 14.0 km via the CTE southbound (EV-TRIP-00107). The GPS trace EV-GPS-00107 records 17.57 km driven, an excess of 3.57 km, or 25.5% of optimal. That passes both POL-RD-01 tests (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not a MATERIAL deviation (25.5% under 50%; 3.57 km under 8.0 km), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged: no full-refund uplift and no conduct referral, and the driver's record shows no repeat pattern (deviation_flags_90d = 1 over 619 completed trips in 90 days). The driver's explanation that the CTE was jammed carries no weight: no traffic advisory exists for this trip (EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0), and under POL-RD-13 an uncited traffic excuse does not reduce the excess and supplies no amended optimal route.\n\nThe arithmetic, had a ruling issued. POL-RD-02 on a METERED fare: recomputed fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 × 14.0 + 0.28 × 24.0) × 1.35) + 0.80 = (3.80 + 10.50 + 6.72) × 1.35 + 0.80 = 28.377 + 0.80 = SGD 29.177; charged_total = SGD 36.60; refund = 36.60 − 29.177 = SGD 7.423, rounded up to SGD 7.45. The 1.35 surge multiplier was read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-00107 and from nowhere else. No ERP, toll, surcharge, promo or waiting-time lines apply, and 7.45 is above the SGD 0.50 de-minimis and below 90% of charged_total.\n\nWhy that refund cannot issue now. POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at the weight of the artifact carrying the deciding fact. The deciding fact is the excess distance, and it is carried by EV-GPS-00107 alone, tagged IMPAIRED at weight 0.30 with issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED (a 331.8 m multipath outlier at 21:44:57, accuracy 42 m, on the Raffles Place approach). The other distance figures are not independent: the trip record's 17.6 km is a rounded copy of the same measurement (POL-RD-01 forbids citing it for the threshold test), and the fare breakdown's 17.60 km is the meter derived from the same trace — one measurement in three artifacts, not three carriers. The chat log and the driver's statement show the route taken, not the distance, and a counterparty statement carries no weight multiplier, so it cannot raise the cap. Confidence is therefore capped at 0.30, below the 0.70 floor, and POL-RD-10(1) makes escalation mandatory and terminal.\n\nBoth things about the trace, as required. It IS down-weighted for admissibility (0.30; GPS_DRIFT, IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED), and it is NOT impaired for policy under POL-RD-07 — max gap 0.0 s, no jump over 500 m (331.8 m), sampling interval 10 s. The deviation may therefore be established on it, and it is; the impairment bites only on confidence.\n\nOn the rider's corroboration and the driver's answer. POL-RD-08's added corroboration requirement (rider profile: 5 deviation claims in 60 days, 1 substantiated; excess under 30%) is met — but not by the billed distance, which is a copy of the trace. It is met by the driver's own admission of the route in his statement (\"I went by Newton and Kim Seng\"), which is on the POL-RD-07(ii) list. That admission does not raise the confidence cap, because it carries no weight multiplier.\n\nWhat would resolve it. An independent measurement of the trip's actual distance — a corrected trace free of the outlier, or a platform-derived billing or telematics source independent of this trace — would bring the confidence cap to the 0.70 floor and allow the SGD 7.45 refund to issue. No referrals are made: POL-RD-06(c) does not fire (no repeat pattern) and POL-RD-09(4) does not fire (ERP is empty and no charge line is unmatched)."
  },
