    "explanation": "To both parties, on trip TRP-00107 (Ang Mo Kio to One Raffles Place, evening of 18 July 2026).\n\n1. Deviation established (rider claim 1; and driver claim 1, which agrees the establishment tests pass). The governing distance is the GPS trace, 17.57 km on EV-GPS-00107, not the rounded 17.6 km on the trip record, which POL-RD-01 forbids for the threshold test. Against the booked optimal of 14.0 km (EV-TRIP-00107, 'CTE southbound throughout') the excess is 3.57 km, or 25.5%; both POL-RD-01 tests (over 20% and over 0.8 km) pass, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not MATERIAL (25.5% is under 50% and 3.57 km is under 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check and the POL-RD-06(b) uplift are not engaged. On the citable counters no repeat pattern exists - deviation_flags_90d is 1 over 619 completed trips, far under the 3-flag and 0.05-ratio triggers (driver claim 2) - so no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises.\n\n2. The driver's traffic excuse does not answer the case. No traffic advisory exists for this trip: EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, null payload. Under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08 the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run, and the assertion that the CTE was jammed carries no weight - it neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal. The driver named no advisory identifier, so the missing advisory is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact under POL-RD-10(5), and the case does not escalate on that ground.\n\n3. EV-GPS-00107 is schema-impaired but NOT policy-impaired, and both things must be said. It carries weight_multiplier 0.30 with issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED (a 331.8 m multipath outlier at 21:44:57 in the Raffles Place urban canyon, accuracy degrading to 42 m, implying 193.6/238.9 kph). That is a schema down-weight only: POL-RD-07 asks for a gap over 90 s (max gap 0.0), a jump over 500 m (331.8 m is under) or a sustained interval over 30 s (10 s), and none is present. The trace is therefore fully usable and the deviation is established on it.\n\n4. The impairment does not push confidence below the 0.70 floor, because the excess is not carried by the trace alone (driver claim 3 rejected; rider claim 2 accepted in outcome but not in reasoning). I do NOT accept that the fare breakdown's 17.60 km on EV-FARE-00107 is an independent carrier: it is the same measurement rounded, and POL-RD-07(ii) records that this platform's meter is derived from the same trace, so a trace and a fare ledger computed from it corroborate nothing, and the trip record's 17.6 km is a rounded copy POL-RD-01 forbids. But the driver's own contemporaneous admission does carry the deviation independently: in the chat log at 21:26, inside the disputed window (EV-CHAT-00107, weight 1.0), the driver answered the rider's query about the Whitley exit by justifying the route rather than disputing it. Under POL-GEN-02(2), where independent artifacts carry the deciding fact the cap is the MAXIMUM of their weights, so the cap is 1.0, not the trace's 0.30, and no POL-RD-10(1) escalation follows. The counterparty statement also admits the route but carries no weight_multiplier, so it neither lifts nor lowers the cap; it is enough to meet the POL-RD-08 corroboration requirement, which draws on the POL-RD-07(ii) list. The rider's profile counters (deviation_claims_60d 5, substantiated 1) license closer scrutiny but, under POL-RD-08 and POL-GEN-01, may never deny an otherwise proven claim, and the required corroboration is present.\n\n5. Refund (rider claim 3). POL-RD-02 runs against the booked optimal route. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + 0.80 = 29.177, the surge multiplier 1.35 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-00107 and nowhere else; there are no ERP, toll, airport-surcharge, waiting-time or promo lines to add or subtract. charged_total is 36.60, so the refund is 36.60 - 29.177 = 7.423, rounded UP to SGD 7.45. It clears the SGD 0.50 de-minimis floor and is 20.3% of charged_total, below the 90% full-refund share. No off-route ERP or phantom charge line exists to correct under POL-RD-09, so no billing-integrity referral arises.\n\nOutcome: PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 7.45 to the rider; the driver is owed no compensation (billed 17.60 km is not less than the trace's 17.57 km, so the POL-RD-04 compensation limb is not met), and there is no clause-mandated referral."
